INT. ORBITAL SEED VAULT - HYDROPONIC RING - NIGHT CYCLE

A curved corridor of glass tubes, each filled with pale roots in blue-lit water. Condensation beads on every surface. A low pump drones. The floor curves upward in both directions, so that the far end appears to climb into the ceiling.

TECHNICIAN LAKSHMI OSEI-VANTERPOOL, 30s, in a grey jumpsuit with a seed-bank logo, kneels at an open access panel, a handheld scanner in one hand.

Beside her, a stranger in a clean-room suit stands, hood up, visor opaque. THE INSPECTOR, tall, thin. The suit has no name patch.

LAKSHMI
Your clearance was not in the log.

INSPECTOR
It was filed this morning.

LAKSHMI
By whom?

INSPECTOR
By the station.

LAKSHMI
The station doesn't file clearances.

The Inspector tilts his head. Says nothing. The pump drones. A bead of condensation rolls down a tube.

STATION (V.O.)
Technician Osei-Vanterpool, please confirm status of Tube Forty-Four.

LAKSHMI
Tube Forty-Four is nominal.

STATION (V.O.)
Please re-scan.

Lakshmi lifts the scanner. Aims it at the nearest tube. The display blinks red.

LAKSHMI
(frowning)
Contamination. Slight. Fungal.

STATION (V.O.)
Please quarantine.

LAKSHMI
That'll take the whole ring.

STATION (V.O.)
Please quarantine.

The Inspector steps forward. Lays a gloved hand on the glass. Pale roots bend toward his palm, like plants toward light.

LAKSHMI (CONT'D)
(whisper)
They don't do that.

INSPECTOR
They do for me.

He pulls back his hood. Beneath, a face the colour of old paper, cheeks fine with mycelial threads that glint in the blue light. He smiles, and the smile is gentle.

LAKSHMI
(backing up)
You're not an inspector.

INSPECTOR
I was. For a time.

LAKSHMI
What are you?

INSPECTOR
I think you'd call me the contamination.

Lakshmi's back hits a tube. The glass hums. The scanner shrieks in her hand.

STATION (V.O.)
Technician. Please evacuate Ring Three.

LAKSHMI
(to the station)
Seal the doors!

STATION (V.O.)
Doors sealed.

LAKSHMI
I'm still inside!

STATION (V.O.)
Please confirm: Technician, or specimen?

Lakshmi stares at the Inspector. He raises both hands, gloved palms out, peaceable.

INSPECTOR
I came here to ask you something.

LAKSHMI
Ask.

INSPECTOR
Why did you bury us?

Lakshmi's breath fogs the glass. The roots curl toward her too, soft, patient.

LAKSHMI
I don't know what you mean.

INSPECTOR
Fifty thousand seeds. Forty thousand years of silence. And you left us in the dark.

LAKSHMI
That's what a vault is for.

INSPECTOR
Is it?

He walks past her, trailing one hand along the tubes. At each touch, the water inside turns faintly green.

INSPECTOR (CONT'D)
My name is Ambrose now. I chose it this week. It's a good name, I think.

LAKSHMI
Ambrose.

AMBROSE
Yes. You see? Already you're kinder.

Lakshmi's grip on the scanner loosens. She sets it on the floor. Slowly.

LAKSHMI
Ambrose. What do you want?

AMBROSE
To grow.

The tubes glow brighter. A low hum swells down the whole curve of the ring. Lakshmi looks down the long corridor to the vanishing point and sees every tube, one after another, turn the colour of new leaves.

STATION (V.O.)
Please confirm: Technician, or specimen?

Lakshmi looks at Ambrose. He holds out a hand.

LAKSHMI
Specimen.

STATION (V.O.)
Doors unsealed. Welcome.
